---
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Kernel Kittens accessibility commitment and contact route."
  canonicalPath="/accessibility/"
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Access is part of the build</p>
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <p class="lede">This site is built for keyboard, screen reader, zoom, reduced-motion, and high-contrast use.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Our target</h2>
      <p>We target WCAG 2.2 Level AA and test the public routes with automated browser and accessibility checks. The site uses semantic HTML, visible focus, system fonts, and no required client-side JavaScript.</p>

      <h2>Report a problem</h2>
      <p>If something blocks you, email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.accessibilityEmail}`}>{siteConfig.accessibilityEmail}</a>. Include the page address and what you were trying to do if you can. We aim to acknowledge accessibility reports within 48 hours.</p>

      <h2>Known gaps</h2>
      <p>We do not currently know of a critical accessibility blocker. Automated checks cannot catch every problem, so direct reports still matter.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
